            {
              "id": "glog-a1245461-f8dd-4a75-880e-3176fe106922",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nCVE-2021-41197 is a vulnerability identified in TensorFlow, a popular open-source machine learning library, specifically affecting version 2.1.0. This vulnerability arises from improper validation of user input, which can lead to a denial of service (DoS) or potentially allow for arbitrary code execution. The issue is rooted in the way TensorFlow handles certain operations, where insufficient checks on input data can cause the application to crash or behave unexpectedly.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: The most effective way to address this vulnerability is to upgrade to a version of TensorFlow where the issue has been fixed. Check the TensorFlow GitHub repository or official announcements for the latest secure version.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement robust input validation to ensure that all inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds and types. This can prevent malformed data from triggering the vulnerability.\n\n3. **Use Security Tools**: Employ static analysis and other security tools to detect and prevent similar vulnerabilities in your codebase.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific fix for this vulnerability involves adding proper checks to ensure that inputs are validated before being processed. Here is a general example of how input validation can be implemented:\n\n```python\ndef safe_tensorflow_operation(input_data):\n    # Example check: Ensure input is a non-empty list of numbers\n    if not isinstance(input_data, list) or not input_data:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-empty list\")\n    if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in input_data):\n        raise ValueError(\"All elements in the input list must be numbers\")\n\n    # Proceed with TensorFlow operations\n    # ...\n\n# Example usage\ntry:\n    safe_tensorflow_operation(user_input)\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f\"Input validation error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheet Series](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2021-41197/pkg:pypi/tensorflow@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
            },
