            {
              "id": "glog-ee471e9d-bf1f-4b33-9233-ebe65d4146bc",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2022-35965** affects the `tensorflow` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the `SparseCountSparseOutput` operation of TensorFlow, where the implementation does not properly validate the input arguments. This can lead to a heap buffer overflow, potentially allowing an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by crashing the application.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. Check the TensorFlow GitHub repository or PyPI for the latest secure version.\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement additional input validation in your application to ensure that all inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds.\n3. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to your dependencies to protect against known vulnerabilities.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe fix for this vulnerability involves adding proper validation checks for the input arguments in the `SparseCountSparseOutput` operation. Ensure that the indices and values are within the expected range and handle any out-of-bound errors gracefully.\n\n```python\n# Example of input validation in TensorFlow operation\nimport tensorflow as tf\n\ndef safe_sparse_count_sparse_output(indices, values, dense_shape):\n    # Validate indices and values\n    if not (0 <= indices < dense_shape).all():\n        raise ValueError(\"Indices are out of bounds\")\n    if not (0 <= values < dense_shape).all():\n        raise ValueError(\"Values are out of bounds\")\n    \n    # Proceed with the operation\n    return tf.raw_ops.SparseCountSparseOutput(\n        indices=indices,\n        values=values,\n        dense_shape=dense_shape\n    )\n```\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to **CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write**. More information can be found on the [CWE website](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2022-35965/pkg:pypi/tensorflow@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
            },
