            {
              "id": "glog-e5046d4c-1f92-44e0-9964-a2e67e675d68",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29604** affects the `tensorflow` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the `SparseCountSparseOutput` operation, where the implementation does not properly validate the input arguments. This can lead to a heap buffer overflow, potentially allowing an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by crashing the application.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. The TensorFlow team has addressed this issue in later versions, so upgrading to the latest stable release is advised.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement additional input validation checks in your application to ensure that all inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds and types.\n\n3. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to your dependencies to protect against known vulnerabilities.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TensorFlow maintainers have fixed this issue in later versions by adding proper input validation checks. If you are unable to upgrade, consider backporting the fix by adding similar validation logic to your local version of the library. Here is a conceptual example of how input validation might be added:\n\n```python\ndef safe_sparse_count_sparse_output(input_tensor):\n    # Example validation logic\n    if not isinstance(input_tensor, tf.SparseTensor):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a SparseTensor\")\n    \n    # Additional checks can be added here\n    # ...\n\n    # Proceed with the operation\n    return tf.raw_ops.SparseCountSparseOutput(input_tensor=input_tensor)\n```\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to **CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write**. More information can be found on the [CWE website](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
