            {
              "id": "glog-13e5fed3-9817-4293-8710-1dbddb2c0eb4",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nCVE-2021-37654 is a vulnerability identified in TensorFlow, a popular open-source machine learning library available on PyPI. This vulnerability affects version 2.1.0 of TensorFlow. The issue arises from improper validation of user input, which can lead to a denial of service (DoS) or potentially allow for arbitrary code execution. The vulnerability is triggered when a maliciously crafted input is processed by the affected functions, leading to unexpected behavior or crashes.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, users should:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to the latest stable version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability has been patched. As of the latest information, versions after 2.1.0 have addressed this issue.\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that only properly formatted data is processed by TensorFlow functions.\n3. **Environment Isolation**: Run TensorFlow applications in isolated environments (e.g., containers) to limit the impact of potential exploits.\n4. **Monitor and Log**: Continuously monitor and log application behavior to detect any anomalies that might indicate exploitation attempts.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific fix for this vulnerability involves adding proper checks and validations in the affected functions to ensure that inputs are within expected bounds and formats. Here is a general example of how input validation can be improved:\n\n```python\ndef safe_function(input_data):\n    # Example of input validation\n    if not isinstance(input_data, expected_type):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid input type\")\n    if not valid_range(input_data):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input out of valid range\")\n    \n    # Proceed with processing\n    process(input_data)\n```\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheet Series](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to CWE-20: Improper Input Validation. More information can be found on the [CWE website](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2021-37654/pkg:pypi/tensorflow@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
