              "id": "glog-7f858765-3550-4438-83bb-770770c36cec",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\n**CVE-2013-2473** is a vulnerability found in the Java Runtime Environment (JRE) component of Oracle Java SE. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to affect confidentiality, integrity, and availability via unknown vectors related to the 2D component. The issue arises from improper handling of certain image data, which can lead to a denial of service or potentially allow for remote code execution.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Update Java**: Ensure that you are using the latest version of Java, as Oracle regularly releases patches for known vulnerabilities.\r\n2. **Restrict Network Access**: Limit network access to systems running Java applications to trusted users and networks.\r\n3. **Use Security Manager**: Enable the Java Security Manager to restrict the permissions of Java applications.\r\n4. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to prevent malicious data from being processed by the application.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nWhile the specific source code fix for this vulnerability is not publicly available, general best practices for handling similar vulnerabilities include:\r\n\r\n- **Validate Image Data**: Ensure that any image data processed by the application is validated for size, format, and content before processing.\r\n- **Use Safe Libraries**: Utilize well-maintained libraries for image processing that are known to handle edge cases and malformed data safely.\r\n- **Error Handling**: Implement robust error handling to gracefully manage unexpected data or processing errors.\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- **CWE-20: Improper Input Validation**: This vulnerability is related to improper input validation, which can lead to various security issues, including denial of service and remote code execution. More details can be found at [CWE-20](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2013-2473/suse:java:"
