              "id": "glog-c88451dd-b7f9-4cc5-84c4-748ab7c16ead",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\nCVE-2013-2454 is a vulnerability in the Java Runtime Environment (JRE) component of Oracle Java SE. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to affect confidentiality, integrity, and availability via unknown vectors related to the Java Runtime Environment. It is a type of security vulnerability that can be exploited by attackers to execute arbitrary code on the affected system.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Update Java**: Ensure that you are using the latest version of Java. Oracle regularly releases updates that patch known vulnerabilities.\r\n2. **Restrict Permissions**: Limit the permissions of Java applications to the minimum necessary for them to function.\r\n3. **Network Security**: Use firewalls and intrusion detection systems to monitor and block suspicious activities.\r\n4. **Disable Unnecessary Features**: Disable Java in web browsers if it is not required, as this can reduce the attack surface.\r\n5. **Security Tools**: Use security tools and software to scan and detect vulnerabilities in your system.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nWhile the specific source code fix for CVE-2013-2454 is not publicly detailed due to its nature as a proprietary vulnerability, general best practices for preventing similar vulnerabilities include:\r\n\r\n- **Input Validation**: Ensure that all inputs are validated and sanitized to prevent injection attacks.\r\n- **Code Review**: Conduct regular code reviews to identify and fix potential security issues.\r\n- **Use Security Libraries**: Utilize well-maintained security libraries and frameworks that provide built-in protection against common vulnerabilities.\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/): A list of the top ten most critical web application security risks.\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html): This CWE is relevant as it involves ensuring that inputs are properly validated to prevent exploitation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2013-2454/suse:java:"
                ]
              }
