            {
              "id": "glog-107d8e05-e118-48e7-a886-15e8b93940f2",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29573** affects the `tensorflow-gpu` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, which is a part of the TensorFlow library. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the implementation of the `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` operation. The operation does not properly validate its input, which can lead to a heap buffer overflow. This can potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by crashing the application.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. The TensorFlow team has addressed this issue in later releases, so upgrading to the latest stable version is advised.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement additional input validation checks in your application to ensure that inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds and types.\n\n3. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to your dependencies to protect against known vulnerabilities.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TensorFlow team has provided a fix for this vulnerability in later versions. The fix involves adding proper validation checks to ensure that the input to `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` is correctly handled. If you are maintaining a fork or cannot upgrade, consider backporting the fix from the official TensorFlow repository.\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- **OWASP Resources**:\n  - [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n  - [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n- **Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)**:\n  - [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\nThese resources provide additional guidance on secure coding practices and understanding common software weaknesses."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2021-29573/pkg:pypi/tensorflow-gpu@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
