              "id": "glog-6c740432-9f39-4cfd-b49d-6e0d75cc97cd",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\nCVE-2015-4803 is a vulnerability found in the Java package management system, `pkg`, which is part of the OpenSolaris operating system. This vulnerability arises from improper handling of package metadata, which can lead to arbitrary code execution. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by crafting a malicious package that, when processed by the `pkg` system, executes arbitrary code with the privileges of the user running the package management commands.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Update and Patch**: Ensure that your system is updated with the latest security patches provided by the vendor. Regularly check for updates to the `pkg` system and apply them promptly.\r\n\r\n2. **Least Privilege Principle**: Run package management commands with the least privileges necessary. Avoid using administrative accounts unless absolutely required.\r\n\r\n3. **Validate Packages**: Only install packages from trusted sources. Verify the integrity and authenticity of packages before installation.\r\n\r\n4. **Monitor and Audit**: Regularly monitor and audit system logs for any suspicious activities related to package management operations.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nTo address this vulnerability, developers should ensure that the `pkg` system properly validates and sanitizes all package metadata before processing. This includes:\r\n\r\n- Implementing strict input validation to ensure that metadata conforms to expected formats and does not contain malicious payloads.\r\n- Using secure coding practices to prevent buffer overflows and other common vulnerabilities that could be exploited through malformed metadata.\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is related to [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2015-4803/suse:java:"
                ]
              }
