                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2020-15203** affects the `tensorflow` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability arises from improper validation of user input, which can lead to a denial of service (DoS) or potentially allow for arbitrary code execution. The issue is rooted in the way TensorFlow handles certain operations, where insufficient checks on input data can cause the application to crash or behave unexpectedly.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability has been addressed. Check the TensorFlow release notes for the version where the fix was applied.\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that all inputs are sanitized and conform to expected formats and ranges.\n3. **Use Security Tools**: Employ static analysis tools to detect potential vulnerabilities in your codebase.\n4. **Monitor Dependencies**: Regularly check for updates and patches for all dependencies, especially those that are critical to your application.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nWhile the specific code changes for the fix are not detailed in the CVE report, a general approach to addressing such vulnerabilities includes:\n\n- Adding checks to validate input dimensions and types before processing.\n- Ensuring that all operations that could potentially lead to buffer overflows or memory corruption are safeguarded with appropriate bounds checking.\n\n### Relevant Links\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE-20: Improper Input Validation)](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\n\nThese resources provide further guidance on secure coding practices and understanding common vulnerabilities."
