              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29538** affects the `tensorflow` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` operation, where the implementation does not properly validate the input arguments. This can lead to a heap buffer overflow, potentially allowing an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by crashing the application.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. The TensorFlow team has addressed this issue in later versions, so upgrading to the latest stable release is advised.\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement additional input validation checks in your application to ensure that inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds.\n3. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to your dependencies to protect against known vulnerabilities.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TensorFlow maintainers have fixed this issue in later versions by adding proper validation checks for the input arguments to the `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` operation. If you are unable to upgrade, consider backporting the fix from the TensorFlow repository to your version. The fix involves:\n\n- Adding checks to ensure that the input tensors are not empty and have valid dimensions.\n- Ensuring that the indices provided do not exceed the bounds of the tensors.\n\n### Relevant Links\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-787](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\nThese resources provide additional guidance on secure coding practices and understanding common vulnerabilities."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2021-29538/pkg:pypi/tensorflow@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
